  biomeName: Archipelago Needles
  minDepthMeters: -200
  maxDepthMeters: 0
  shortDescription: Razor-sharp limestone spires rising from the surf. Wind-eroded
    bird-nesting pillars with salt-crusted peaks.
  isPlaceholder: 0
  visitPurpose: Early exploration biome. Come here to learn routes, gather basics,
    and follow strong natural shapes and search obvious pockets.
  commonRewardHook: Common runs pay out in Titanium Scrap and Silica Shards.
  rareRewardHook: 'Rare pull is modest: Fiber Kelp and Glass Panel.'
  landmarkIdentity: Archipelago Needles reads through spires, steps, and big natural
    crowns. Landmarks should feel bright and readable.
  safePocketIdentity: Safe pockets are frequent. The player should often see a clear
    reset point nearby.
  riskSummary: 'Main failure mode: bad drops and exposed lines. Creature pressure
    stays low.'
  extractionFocus: 'Loose pickup fields and readable shallow mineral nodes. Early
    tier: keep runs short and favor stone pockets and hard-form nodes.'
  landmarkGuidance: Dominant landmark is karst arch or sea-stack crown. This slot
    should read through small limestone teeth and arch feet; use vertical forms to
    keep heading.
